# gr0b.skill — optional agent skill file
#
# Drop this file into your agent's skills directory so it automatically
# follows the gr0b memory protocol every session.
#
# Claude Code:  copy to ~/.claude/skills/gr0b.skill
# Gemini:       copy to ~/.gemini/skills/gr0b.skill
# Cursor:       add as a custom rule in your project .cursorrules
#
# This file is OPTIONAL — gr0b works without it. The skill makes the
# session-log habit explicit and automatic rather than relying on the
# agent inferring it from CLAUDE.md.

---
name: gr0b
description: >
  Persistent brain protocol — read memory on session start, write a session
  log on session end, and use graphify + agentmemory for cross-session recall.
triggers:
  - on_session_start
  - on_session_end

on_session_start: |
  ## gr0b — Session Start

  1. Read `~/.gr0b/index.md` to orient yourself: what projects exist, what
     agents have been active, and what open threads remain.

  2. Check `~/.gr0b/session-logs/<agent>/` for logs from recent sessions
     relevant to the current task. Prioritise the last 3–5.

  3. If the task involves a specific codebase, run:
         graphify query "<brief description of what you're working on>"
     from the project root. This gives you a semantically grounded map of
     the relevant code communities before you start exploring files.

  4. If you need facts from previous sessions across all agents, use:
         agentmemory recall "<query>"

on_session_end: |
  ## gr0b — Session End

  Write a session log before closing. Path:
      ~/.gr0b/session-logs/<agent>/YYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM.md

  Template:
  ```markdown
  # Session — YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM

  ## What was worked on
  <!-- One paragraph summary -->

  ## Key decisions made
  <!-- Bullet list of meaningful choices and their rationale -->

  ## Files changed
  <!-- Paths relative to project root -->

  ## Open threads / next steps
  <!-- What remains, what to pick up next session -->
  ```

  Keep it brief — the goal is context recovery, not documentation for its
  own sake. Future-you will thank present-you.

notes: |
  - Session logs are plain markdown. Open `~/.gr0b` as an Obsidian vault
    to get a graph view across all your sessions and agents.
  - BRAIN_MAP.md (regenerate: `python3 ~/.gr0b/scripts/gr0b_map.py`) gives
    a high-level map of your codebase communities.
  - agentmemory runs on port 3111. Start it with:
        npx @agentmemory/agentmemory
  - graphify watches your Desktop folder for changes. Check the watcher:
        launchctl list | grep gr0b   (macOS)
        Get-ScheduledTask gr0b*      (Windows)
